diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index d17b3da6b..1dac70cb8 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -278,6 +278,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5916+) **Minimum worker production floor**: AI cities now rebuild toward an area-local worker minimum (2 workers for the capital area, 1 per other city) before normal production priorities can keep winning indefinitely. This makes **early worker availability** much more reliable **after losses or underproduction**, **improving early development** because workers are **high-value relative to their cost**, especially when larger cities can produce them with **food + hammers**. The floor does not force only high-pop/capital cities to build workers, because weaker or stagnant cities can sometimes contribute without interrupting stronger cities' growth or key builds. This higher worker production is also beneficial throughout the game. Worker **scrapping** uses the same shared floor so later quota tuning cannot accidentally scrap below the rebuild minimum.
 - Greatly simplified `AI_betterPlotBuild`: hard **de-prioritization of roads/routes** early; build them only when they’re truly the best move. Focus is on **yields first**, but still ensure **important bonus connections** (road/route when the bonus is connectable and not yet connected). See [KI#31](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#31---attemptingly-fixed-deprioritize-routes-for-ai-workers-in-favour-of-yields-first-except-in-some-rare-cases).
 - **Overhaul: `AI_bestCityBuild` (full routine):** "holy" improvements (never overwrite: **hamlet, village, town, workshop**) and "semi-holy" (contextual: **farms** in food-poor cities, **cottages** in food-rich cities); fast/ordered improvement; **bonus-specific rules** (e.g., don’t cottage bananas; prefer plantation or a farm only if it makes clear sense); **terrain-aware cottage/farm logic** (flood plains favored for cottages unless the city is food-poor); **minimal oscillation**; prefer steady growth; avoid overwriting until other workable tiles are improved; hold top tiles for later if the "now" move would be inferior; prefer farms on low-food BFCs. See [KI#33](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#33---tremendously-improved-and-fixed-and-enhanced-ai-worker-buildimprovement-logic-in-cvunitaiai_bestcitybuild). Update: worker AI now also weighs the **longer-term value** of strong **non-bonus farms** for **low-food or hill-heavy cities**: they can **support food-consuming mines**, **faster growth**, **more aggressive early slaving**, or **specialist economies**; (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5914+) concrete dry-farm irrigation-chain fixes can replace the least harmful blocker first; and the logic is more **mindful of preserving useful irrigation paths** instead of blindly maximizing immediate cottage/workshop yield ((Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5926+) **Reserve** likely irrigation/farm connector plots **from non-farm builds** to reduce AI worker farm/non-farm oscillation).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5949+) **Worker lower-food replacement guard:** from a **tunable era onward** (default as of now: Medieval), AI workers no longer replace existing **no-bonus** improvements with lower-food alternatives. This targets **repeated food-threshold oscillation** such as **Farm → Cottage → Farm → Cottage** or **Mine → Windmill → Mine** after the city briefly looks food-safe. It still allows equal-food retools, food-restoration changes such as Cottage → Farm, and cleanup of City Ruins or obsolete/non-active improvements. In the tested BBAI log, the worst Mali farm/cottage loops reached Farm again and then skipped later Farm → Cottage attempts from about T128/T130 onward. This change is because before this era, cities are often small or health/happiness-capped (extra/excess food may not necessarily help or could be inefficient early) and early cottages still have time to mature, but later, cities are usually larger, health sources are generally multiple, and specialist yields are stronger than plot yields (so any food can be used and is generally strong/stronger), and cottages/growth improvements have less time to grow and pay back, so preserving food support is usually stronger.
 - **Feature-removal health handling in `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild`:** forests provide city health, so non-bonus forest chops are **weighted by city population and health surplus**; **small cities** can still chop, but when health is tight the AI usually **prefers other useful improvements** because removing forest health can make the city unhealthy or more unhealthy. **Jungle is different** because it **adds unhealth** and is **generally targeted** for removal/improvement. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5941+) For **medium/large cities**, non-bonus forested BFC plots have a **softer health penalty**. This is because later in the game we usually have many health sources (trade, owned bonuses, buildings, techs, etc.), **higher population** can use or needs more improved BFC plots, and **improved yields are stronger**, so leaving useful forested tiles unimproved forever can be worse than accepting the forest-health loss.
 - **Mobility:** workers leave "over-improved" cities sooner to help weaker ones; later pass further improves cross-city mobility and bravery within borders (less idle parking). See [KI#39](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#39---seemingly-fixed-orand-enhanced-make-ai-workers-move-sooner-to-city-b-or-city-c-or-such-and-vice-versa-if-current-city-is-already-improved-enough-and-dont-need-to-be-over-improved-while-other-cities-are-not-improved-enough-and-would-much-rather-need-it) and [KI#41](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#41---seemingly-fixed-beyond-tremendously-improved-ai-worker-mobility-flexibility-and-reliability-now-favouring-minimal-big-city-improvement-come-back-to-it-later-but-dont-delay-improving-smaller-ones-quick-moving-to-smaller-ones-and-spending-longer-to-improve-smaller-ones-as-they-grow-fast-but-as-well-as-being-braver-in-our-own-cultural-borders-orand-moving-to-other-cities-needing-improvements-rather-than-being-parked-in-current-city-if-i-am-not-mistaken-but-and-such-other-changes-to-increase-ai-efficiency-reliably-and-other-changes-if-any-thanks-to-chatgpt-5-and-me-too-if-i-may-say-but).
 - Update: **AI workers: favor low-pop cities (untested in a before/after save file compare):** `CvUnitAI::AI_nextCityToImprove` now weights smaller cities higher so workers rotate to underdeveloped hubs sooner—spreading early tile improvements, jump-starting growth, and avoiding over-investment in already-strong capitals. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5938+) Update 2: **Worker mobility / overimprovement refinement:** workers still rotate away from sufficiently improved small cities, but medium and large cities are less likely to leave useful BFC plots unimproved. Workers also avoid ordinary replacement churn (e.g., **Mine ↔ Windmill**, **Cottage ↔ Farm**) ((Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5944+) unless there is no other pathable and unreserved unimproved BFC improvement candidate for this worker), while valid unimproved BFC work remains, except for bonus fixes and irrigation-chain farms. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5942+) Update 3: the small-city rotation shortcut no longer makes a worker leave **if it is already standing on this same city's owned/workable non-home BFC plot** and `AI_bestCityBuild` selects that plot as the current best local build. This fixed or reduced cases like workers roading a useful forested or otherwise improvable plot and then walking away instead of finishing the chop/improvement, then leaving it unimproved late in the game.

